            <ArticleTitle>Hydrogen sulphide poisoning: associated with pelt processing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>145-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Four cases of poisoning with hydrogen sulphide (H2S) were admitted to Ashburton Hospital within a period of one week following accidental exposure to H2S at a freezing works. We review the clinical presentation of these four cases, their management, follow up and the circumstances which led to their accidental exposure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
